{"name":"Spring Day","hex":"#dbd7b7","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spring","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To move or burst forth.","To appear."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of springing: a leap, a jump.","The season of the year in temperate regions in which temperatures and daylight hours rise, and plants spring from the ground and into bloom and dormant animals spring to life."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spring"},{"term":"day","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Symbol","definitions":["ISO 639-2 & ISO 639-5 language code for Land Dayak languages."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The time when the Sun is above the horizon and it lights the sky.","A period of time equal or almost equal to a full day-night cycle, being 24 hours long."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/day"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spring day","blocks":[{"text":"Spring Day is a holiday marking the coming of the spring season, which takes place in different countries, on varying dates."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_day","wikidata":"Q3305281"},{"title":"Spring (season)","blocks":[{"text":"Spring, also known as springtime, is one of the four temperate seasons, succeeding winter and preceding summer. There are various technical definitions of spring, but local usage of the term varies according to local climate, cultures and customs. When it is spring in the Northern Hemisphere, it is autumn in the Southern Hemisphere and vice versa. At the spring equinox, also called the vernal equinox, days and nights are approximately twelve hours long, with daytime length increasing and nighttime length decreasing as the season progresses until the summer solstice. The spring equinox is in March in the Northern Hemisphere and in September in the Southern Hemisphere, while the summer solstice is in June in the Northern Hemisphere and in December in the Southern Hemisphere."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Arboretum_Robert_Lenoir_-_Jardin_des_m%C3%A9llif%C3%A8res.jpg/330px-Arboretum_Robert_Lenoir_-_Jardin_des_m%C3%A9llif%C3%A8res.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_(season)","wikidata":"Q1312"},{"title":"Spring Day (song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Spring Day\" is a song recorded by South Korean boy band BTS for their 2017 album You Never Walk Alone, a repackage of their second Korean-language studio album, Wings (2016). The song was written by \"Hitman\" Bang, RM, Adora, Arlissa Ruppert, Peter Ibsen, Suga, and its producer Pdogg. It was released for digital download and streaming on February 13, 2017, as the album's lead single by Big Hit Entertainment. A remix of the song was subsequently released for free via SoundCloud on June 4, 2018. A Japanese version of the song was issued on May 10, 2017, through Universal Music Japan, as a B-side of the single album that included the tracks \"Blood Sweat & Tears\" and \"Not Today\", both also in Japanese. The song is an alternative hip hop and pop rock power ballad, which relies on rock instrumentation. The lyrics revolve around the themes of loss, longing, grief, and moving on."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spring_Day_(song)","wikidata":"Q31179670"},{"title":"Day","blocks":[{"text":"A day is the time period of a full rotation of the Earth with respect to the Sun. On average, this is 24 hours. As a day passes at a given location it experiences morning, afternoon, evening, and night. This daily cycle drives circadian rhythms in many organisms, which are vital to many life processes."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Day","wikidata":"Q573"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Zjarri.jpg/500px-Zjarri.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/Zjarri.jpg/500px-Zjarri.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Zjarri for the celebration of Dita e Verës in Tropojë, northern Albania. Kindled on the eve or before sunrise in order to give strength to the Sun (Dielli), people dance and sing around it or jump across it, a ritual practiced for the end of winter, renewal, purification and apotropaic purposes.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AZjarri.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Spring_cherry_blossoms_in_Hagley_Park.jpg/500px-Spring_cherry_blossoms_in_Hagley_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Spring_cherry_blossoms_in_Hagley_Park.jpg/1280px-Spring_cherry_blossoms_in_Hagley_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/Spring_cherry_blossoms_in_Hagley_Park.jpg/500px-Spring_cherry_blossoms_in_Hagley_Park.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Cherry blossoms flowering during springtime in Christchurch, New Zealand","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASpring_cherry_blossoms_in_Hagley_Park.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Millettia_peguensis%2C_Moulmein_rosewood%2C_Bengali_-Monimala_with_pink-_purple_small_flower_in_march_2020._Ramna_Park%2C_Dhaka._%282%29.jpg/500px-Millettia_peguensis%2C_Moulmein_rosewood%2C_Bengali_-Monimala_with_pink-_purple_small_flower_in_march_2020._Ramna_Park%2C_Dhaka._%282%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/33/Millettia_peguensis%2C_Moulmein_rosewood%2C_Bengali_-Monimala_with_pink-_purple_small_flower_in_march_2020._Ramna_Park%2C_Dhaka._%282%29.jpg/1280px-Millettia_peguensis%2C_Moulmein_rosewood%2C_Bengali_-Monimala_with_pink-_purple_small_flowe